# Imported INSIDE the {$SITE_DOMAIN} site block, production only.
#
# Mail lives at mail.tatvaos.com and nowhere else. Both hostnames are front
# doors onto the same web container, so without this every product answered on
# every host — core.tatvaos.com/mail/inbox served the app on the wrong domain.
#
# A named matcher + handle: `handle` takes exactly ONE matcher token, so the
# two paths (/mail and everything under it) go in a named matcher first. Using
# a `handle` (not a bare redir) puts this in the same mutually-exclusive group
# as the catch-all `handle { reverse_proxy web:3000 }`; imported before it, this
# matches /mail paths first and redirects deterministically. The path is kept
# ({uri}) and the auth cookie is on .tatvaos.com, so deep links and the session
# both survive the hop.
@mailpaths path /mail /mail/*
handle @mailpaths {
    redir https://{$MAIL_DOMAIN}{uri} 302
}
